# Build context for `deploy/worker/Dockerfile` (the image remote agents run in).
#
# That Dockerfile copies the whole workspace, because cargo loads every
# member's manifest before it builds one package, and it needs
# `vendor/alacritty_terminal` for the same reason. So the context has to carry
# Cargo.toml, Cargo.lock (when a lock file exists; the repository does not track
# one), crates/, apps/desktop (a workspace member) and vendor/.
#
# Everything below is local-only or belongs to another surface, and a local
# `target/` alone is larger than the image — this keeps a CI checkout and a
# developer's machine from sending gigabytes. `deploy/` stays in the context
# because the Dockerfile that a build reads lives in it.

.git
.github
.agents
.config
.grok
.modal

# Local build output and scratch files.
target
**/node_modules
.DS_Store
*.swp
*.swo
*.sqlite
*.sqlite.bak
*.log

# The Expo clients and the landing site: neither is a cargo workspace member.
apps/common
apps/mobile
apps/web
landing
